Based on my analysis of the workspace code, transcripts, and type definitions, I've identified one hallucination — a CSS custom property name that doesn't exist in the media-chrome/mux-player API.

The variable `--media-time-buffered-color` does not exist in the library. The actual documented variable is `--media-time-range-buffered-color` (defined on `media-time-range.d.ts` in media-chrome). Claude wrote both versions side-by-side in the final `src/index.css`, with only the second being valid.

All `::part()` selectors used (bottom, seek-backward, seek-forward, rendition, audio-track, airplay, cast, play, mute, volume, display, captions, playback-rate, pip, fullscreen) are valid — runtime inspection in rung 5 confirmed they match the space-separated part names like `"bottom play button"`. All other CSS variables (`--media-range-thumb-*`, `--media-range-track-background`, `--media-range-bar-color`, `--media-time-range-buffered-color`) are documented in `media-chrome-range.d.ts` / `media-time-range.d.ts`. All MuxPlayer props (playbackId, muted, loop, autoPlay, thumbnailTime, accentColor, ref) are present in the React component's TypeScript types. The earlier use of `--media-control-bar-background` in rung 3 was tested, found ineffective, and removed — so it qualifies as "buggy code Claude then fixed" rather than a hallucination.

